BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Much Ado About Nothing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260807T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260807T193000
UID:260602_Uc2xjHW4UOXrQeYir1Exg
DESCRIPTION:**It’s Shakespeare in the Piazza at Bacchus Landing**!\n\nWh
 ile Claudio and Hero fall in love and get engaged\, the villainous Don Joh
 n tricks Claudio into believing Hero is unfaithful\, leading him to public
 ly humiliate her at the altar. Meanwhile\, their friends conspire to make 
 the sparring Beatrice and Benedick fall in love\, and they eventually conf
 ess their feelings for each other. The play’s climax\, in pure Shakespea
 rean form\, involves a faked death\, a confession of Don John’s plot\, a
 nd a happy ending with a double wedding – of course!\n\nBacchus Landing
 ’s wood-fired pizza will be available for purchase\, and wine by the gla
 ss or bottle will also be available for purchase from selected wineries ea
 ch evening (see the schedule\, below). **Sorry\, no outside food or drink
  allowed except for water bottles.** Remember\, Sonoma County evenings ge
 t chilly even in the summer. We advise you to bring a sweater\, jacket\, o
 r hoodie in case you need to bundle up after sunset!\n\nJuly 23rd\, 24th\,
  25th\, 30th\, 31st\; August 1st\, 6th\, 7th. 7:30 pm.\n\nBy William Shake
 speare Directed by Steven David Martin Running time: 2:15 hours Doors open
  at 6:30 pm. **Come early to enjoy Bacchus Landing wood-fired pizza and s
 elect wines!** Free parking is available and the premises are wheelchair-a
 ccessible.
LOCATION:Bacchus Landing 
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/much-ado-about-nothing/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Road to Appalachia featuring Mark & Maggie O'Connor
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260807T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260807T213000
UID:260523kDjXJe9o2kG67afQXn8Fog
DESCRIPTION:Road to Appalachia featuring Mark & Maggie O’Connor\n\nAugus
 t 7\, 2026\, at 7:30 pm\n\nWeill Hall\, Green Music Center\n\nFrancesco Le
 cce-Chong\, conductor\n\nMark O’Connor\, violin\n\nMaggie O’Connor\, v
 iolin\n\nGABRIELA LENA FRANK: Elegía Andina\n\nAARON COPLAND: Appalachian
  Spring\n\nGABRIELA LENA FRANK: Escaramuza\n\nMARK O'CONNOR:\n\nSong of th
 e Liberty Bell for Violin and String Orchestra\n\nStrings & Threads Suite 
 for Violin and String Orchestra\n\nGRAMMY Award-winning Violinists Mark O'
 Connor and Maggie O'Connor return to Santa Rosa with music that bridges co
 ncert hall tradition and the roots of American sound. Their works Song of 
 the Liberty Bell and Strings & Threads Suite blend classical form with fol
 k melodies and virtuosic fiddling\, creating a vibrant\, living expression
  of American music.\n\nAt the heart of the program is Aaron Copland’s Ap
 palachian Spring\, a landmark of the American repertoire. Premiered in 194
 4 for Martha Graham\, the score captures a sense of optimism and renewal\,
  culminating in the beloved Shaker tune “Simple Gifts.”\n\nWoven throu
 ghout the concert are two striking works by Gabriela Lena Frank Elegía An
 dina and Escaramuza—which draw on Latin American influences to expand an
 d enrich the idea of what “American” music can be.\n\nFrom Appalachian
  landscapes to Andean echoes\, this program traces a musical journey shape
 d by tradition\, migration\, and reinvention—an evolving portrait of a n
 ation in sound.\n\nPrograms\, dates\, artists\, and prices are subject to 
 change without notice. Tickets are subject to availability. All tickets ar
 e nonrefundable.
LOCATION:Green Music Center
URL:https://www.srsymphony.org/event/road-to-appalachia-featuring-mark-mag
 gie-oconnor/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
