BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:National Lighthouse Day 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260807T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260807T210000
UID:260801EL209QY0SkK-bQewFfLrhA
DESCRIPTION:Experience the historic Point Reyes Lighthouse as it appeared 
 a century ago. On this special evening\, Point Reyes National Seashore wil
 l illuminate and rotate the 156-year old Fresnel lens\, giving visitors a 
 rare opportunity to witness history in motion. The Lighthouse Visitor Cent
 er will be open with exhibits\, retail offerings\, and light refreshments 
 for sale. Throughout the evening\, staff will be available to answer quest
 ions\, share the history of the lighthouse\, and provide interpretive prog
 rams for visitors of all ages. Important Event Information:  Carpooling is
  encouraged\, as parking is very limited and may fill early—please plan 
 to arrive ahead of time. The Drakes Beach and South Beach parking lots are
  great options to carpool from.  ADA parking is limited. If you anticipate
  needing an ADA space\, please contact the park in advance to discuss avai
 lability. Bring a flashlight or headlamp\; red‑light options are preferr
 ed to reduce night‑vision disruption. Access to the lighthouse requires 
 a 0.4‑mile walk from the parking lot along a dimly lit pathway and the d
 escent to the lighthouse involves 313 stairs. The lighthouse is also visib
 le from the Observation Deck at the top of the stairs for those who do not
  wish to descend. If wind speeds reach unsafe levels\, the stairs will clo
 se but the Observation Deck will remain open. Weather is frequently windy 
 and cold. Please bring warm layers\, sturdy shoes\, and snacks. Restrooms 
 are available near the Lighthouse Visitor Center and the parking area.
LOCATION:Point Reyes National Seashore
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1227521053776368/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
