BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Beat Farmers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T000000
UID:260612pQ-EIdJ9PUGLfInaAX8pCQ
DESCRIPTION:In August\, 1983\, a yet-to-be-named band begins to play a ser
 ies of unannounced dates at the Spring Valley Inn. For a case of Bud Light
 \, the band gets the name the &quot\;Beat Farmers&quot\;. In January\, 198
 4\, the BFers begin playing Bodies\, a dive bar in San Diego. By March\, t
 hey are signed to Rhino Records for a one album deal. Armed with a $4000 b
 udget\, they record &quot\;Tales Of The New West&quot\; \\(featuring the C
 ountry Dick standard &quot\;Happy Boy&quot\;\\). \n\n \n\n Tales... is rel
 eased in January\, 1985 while the BFers play the Bacchanal in San Diego qu
 ite often. March\, 1985\, the BFers begin their first US tour. After openi
 ng for the Blasters\, they make the mistake of their lives by signing a 7 
 record deal with CURB Records. They take off to England for a 3 week tour 
 in June and record &quot\;Glad 'N Greasy&quot\; for Demon Records. Decembe
 r\, 1985\, Buddy Blue leaves the band after recording &quot\;Van Go&quot\;
  but never waiting around for its release. Joey Harris\, who had worked wi
 th Dick in 1983 with Country Dick and the Snuggle Bunnies. &quot\;Van Go&q
 uot\; is released in June\, 1986 while the band plays two 60\,000 person f
 estivals in Belgium. The song &quot\;Riverside&quot\; gets radio play and 
 the band is asked to make a cheesie Budweiser radio commercial using the m
 usic from &quot\;Riverside&quot\;. \n\n \n\n February\, 1987\, the BFers c
 omplete recording &quot\;The Pursuit Of Happiness&quot\;. The single &quot
 \;Make It Last&quot\; is added to 40 country/western stations in June but 
 as soon as the album is released\, the radio programmers hear the rest of 
 the album and drop the song from the play lists- to much rock and roll. Oc
 tober\, 1987\, Dick almost beats up the lead singer for Duran Duran. &quot
 \;Dark Light&quot\; makes some noise on radio play lists. \n\n \n\n Januar
 y\, 1988\, the BFers begin work on the next album. In May\, 1988\, they st
 art a European tour for two months. They return to deal with label problem
 s. In February\, 1989\, Dick and Joey join Mojo Nixon and Dave Alvin \\(Bl
 asters\\) with nine other tuxedoed fools and play the west coast as &quot\
 ;The Pleasure Barons&quot\;. A live album is recorded an eventually releas
 ed in 1993. In July\, 1989\, &quot\;Poor and Famous&quot\; is finally rele
 ased. While playing their annual New Years shows\, they record the shows f
 or a live album. \n\n \n\n In March\, 1990\, Dick has thyroid surgery. Thi
 s problem has been bothering Dick for years now. He has been in and out of
  the doctor's office for cancer treatments. June\, 1990\, the live album i
 s released\, &quot\;Live\, Loud\, and Plowed&quot\; without the bands know
 ledge. Dick discovers it at a Tower Records in San Diego. They play the Da
 vid Letterman Show in New York. Dave's says he wants to become a roadie fo
 r the band. \n\n \n\n The band fights for the next few years to boot CURB.
  The lawyers get rich and the band continues to play regularly on the west
  coast with various swings to the mid-west and east. \n\n \n\n The BFers c
 ontinue to have various other projects going on including the Incredible H
 ayseeds \\(a country western review show with a trombone added\\)\, Countr
 y Dick's Petting Zoo\, Country Dick's Garage\, Jerry and Joey acoustic\, J
 erry and Buddy jam nights\, and the Pleasure Barons. Country Dick is recor
 ding a solo effort. This will contain many of the nasty Dick songs we all 
 know and love as well as some straight ahead rock and rollers like &quot\;
 Big Fast Town&quot\; and &quot\;Indigo Rider&quot\;. Dick said recently th
 at this will be out someday and is a concept album\, Dick style. Dick is a
 lso working with Mojo Nixon when time permits. \n\n \n\n Undaunted\, the B
 Fers head to Vancouver\, Canada in 1993 to record their new record. The un
 titled album is completed and the band begins the search for a new record 
 label. Sector 2 Records\, out of Austin\, signs the band and soon &quot\; 
 Viking Lullabys&quot\; \\(spelled wrong because Dick likes it that way!\\)
  is pressed up on CD and readied for release on August 9\, 1994. \n\n \n\n
  The band continues to tour \\(what else is new!\\) and then returns to Sa
 n Diego and begins work in early 1995 on a new album. They decide to produ
 ce it themselves and record it in San Diego \\(a first!\\). The Bfers chan
 ge their sound slightly to get a harder sound to this new album. Those bas
 tards at CURB decide to release a greatest hits package in truly cheap for
 m. It is a very poor retrospective of the band that was packaged\, put tog
 ether\, and released without the bands knowledge \\(sound familiar!\\). Oh
  how we love CURB! \n\n \n\n By mid-year\, the album is finished. &quot\; 
 Manifold&quot\; is the title and it is released on September 19\, 1995. As
  a tribute to the home town fans\, the album is released two weeks earlier
  in San Diego to coincide with the Street Scene \\(an outdoor concert even
 t that takes place every year in San Diego\\). The band hits the road with
  the Blasters for a co-headline tour that swings all over the country in S
 eptember and October. \n\n \n\n Suddenly on a Wednesday night\, November 8
 th\, 1995\, while playing drums in Whistler\, Brittish Columbia \\(about o
 ne hour out of Vancouver- a BFer strong hold!\\) the unthinkable happened.
  Country Dick was struck down by a heart attack during the third song of t
 heir show. \n\n \n\n The indestructible\, fun loving\, deep voiced\, frien
 dly\, extremely humorous giant is now gone. There are no words that can de
 scribe how any BFer fan feels. Dan McLain AKA Country Dick Montana was a t
 alent that can never be equaled. Sure he wasn't well known but anyone who 
 ever saw a BFer live show could tell you that Dick was at his best- on sta
 ge. His presence will never be replaced and I know that the remaining BFer
 s do not want to replace him. Whatever shape the BFers take\, it will neve
 r be the same without Country Dick Montana. As of 11/11/95\, the BFers are
  no more.
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern Novato
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1039066062?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sounds of Summer: Liongate Sound Bath Journey San Rafael
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T213000
UID:260803yUsijMRHb0au6tENrwtwag
DESCRIPTION:**Journey Beyond Sound** presents *Sounds of Summer: A Meditat
 ive Sound Bath Journey | Lionsgate Edition* in San Rafael\, an evening of 
 guided meditation and immersive meditative sound inspired by the themes of
  the 8/8 Lionsgate Portal. Relax comfortably as Sean David\, Belinda Salvi
 dge featuring her stunning vintage Parisian violin\, and Sanaz Sounds crea
 te an evolving soundscape with crystal and Tibetan singing bowls\, symphon
 ic gongs\, Native flute\, hand drums\, shamanic rattles\, and other resona
 nt instruments.\n\nNestled in the peaceful hills of Lucas Valley\, this sp
 ecial evening invites you to slow down\, quiet the mind\, and create space
  for reflection\, intention\, and renewal in a warm and welcoming setting.
LOCATION:Church of the Nativity 
URL:https://journeybeyondsound.com/etn/sounds-of-summer-a-meditative-sound
 -bath-journey-lionsgate-edition-san-rafael/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nature's Palette: Hand-Painting Fabric with Botanical Colors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T140000
UID:260803tQrOdpeD9k6tHRi0QNnOsw
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, August 8\, 2026 10:00 AM – 2:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\
 nRedwood Grove\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nEvent Category: Fiber 
 Arts\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration\n\nRegistration Cost:\n
 \n$80\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$40\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$120\n\nDisc
 over rich\, luminous hues while learning to hand-paint fabric using botani
 cal colors. In this beginner-friendly workshop\, you’ll explore simple t
 echniques for applying natural dyes to cloth while creating your own long\
 , narrow runner—perfect for a table or hanging in a window. Working outd
 oors and inspired by the natural world around us\, you’ll gain an introd
 uction to natural dye processes\, color layering\, and handcrafted design.
  Leave with a one-of-a-kind textile and the inspiration to continue explor
 ing natural dyes. No experience required. Feel free to bring a bag lunch o
 r snacks and a beverage to enjoy while you work.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/natures-palette/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
