BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art of Community Festival - Diana Krevsky Opening Reception
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T160000
UID:260728_zbDK1KV6E-wY4DQK6bvgw
DESCRIPTION:We are proud to present the 3rd Annual Art of Community Festiv
 al\, a month-long celebration of creativity\, culture\, and community taki
 ng place throughout August on the historic Mare Island waterfront.\n\nWhat
  began as a grassroots community art exhibition has grown into a dynamic f
 estival that brings together artists\, youth creatives\, makers\, cultural
  organizations\, and community members in a shared celebration of the peop
 le and ideas that make Vallejo unique.\n\nAug 8\, The 2026 Art of Communit
 y Festival proudly presents “Legacy in Color\,” a solo exhibition cele
 brating the work of Bay Area artist Diana Krevsky. Using a variety of medi
 a and materials\, combined with a playful sense of irony\, Krevsky’s wor
 k often explores the conflict between cultural values and individual ident
 ity within both political and natural landscapes. Her paintings and sculpt
 ures are at once colorful\, whimsical\, thought-provoking\, and deeply per
 sonal. Visitors can meet the artist during the festival’s Opening Recept
 ion and Artist Talk at 2 p.m.\n\nAug 9\, Art of Community Awards Honoring 
 individuals and organizations making a meaningful impact through art\, cul
 ture\, and community.\n\nAug 16\, Mare Island Art • Fashion • Vintage 
 Bazaar A waterfront market featuring artists\, makers\, fashion vendors\, 
 vintage dealers\, collectors\, and creative entrepreneurs.\n\nAug 23\, Val
 lejo Youth Artists “Under 21” Exhibition Reception & Poetry Showcase F
 eaturing emerging artists and young creative voices from throughout the re
 gion.
LOCATION:Mare Island Art Studios
URL:https://mareislandartstudios.com/events/art-of-community-festival-2026
 /
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
