BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Drawing Trees in Mixed Media at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T140000
UID:260720f-s6ng-cZ0GeCdbam9F2YQ
DESCRIPTION:Spend a day immersed in the art of drawing trees\, set against
  the inspiring landscape of Jack London State Historic Park. This plein ai
 r workshop blends skill-building with outdoor observation\, helping you de
 epen both your technique and your connection to the natural world.\n\nIn t
 he morning\, focus on foundational drawing principles—learning how to ca
 pture accurate proportions\, simplify complex forms\, and develop a strong
  sense of value.\n\nIn the afternoon\, attention shifts to the expressive 
 qualities of trees\, exploring texture\, color\, and light as observed dir
 ectly from the landscape. Enhance your drawings with watercolor washes\, a
 dding depth\, atmosphere\, and color to bring trees to life. Step-by-step 
 guidance ensures that finished piece reflects both structure and character
 .\n\nBring a picnic lunch for a mid-day break\, and a lightweight folding 
 chair if you have one \\(seating is also available at picnic tables\, benc
 hes\, or on the ground\\). All materials are provided.  Artists of all ex
 perience levels are welcome.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/plein-air-trees-august-2026-copy-cop
 y/
