DESCRIPTION:Don’t be fooled by the title of this play – it’s a comed
 y!\n\nIvan Menchell’s The Cemetery Club is a bittersweet comedy about th
 ree Jewish widows in Queens\, New York\, who meet monthly to visit their h
 usbands' graves. Their routine is upended when one of them  begins dating
  a widower\, who\, they incidentally\, meet at the cemetery. The ensuing d
 rama tests their loyalties\, offering a poignant look at love\, friendship
  and moving on.
LOCATION:Bay Area Stage Theatre on Broadway
URL:https://www.bayareastage.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Sourdough Baking
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260809T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260809T164500
UID:260728vKkx0dOpmE6ReCCl-rjjkw
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, August 9\, 2026\n\n2:00 PM – 4:45 PM\n\nLocation\n\
 nRoom 110\n\nCategory\n\nCulinary Arts\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n
 \nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$100\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n
 $5\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$105\n\nDelve into the delicious art of 
 sourdough baking with our hands-on workshop that aims to demystify the sou
 rdough process and make it more approachable for at-home bakers! This hand
 s-on experience will guide you through each step of the process\, deepenin
 g your understanding of the fundamentals of sourdough and elevating your b
 aking skills to new heights! Learn the secrets behind cultivating and main
 taining a robust starter culture and the key to a deliciously tangy bread.
 Next\, roll up your sleeves as you learn to mix\, knead\, and shape your d
 ough like a pro. Gain insight into the science behind fermentation and glu
 ten development and discover the secrets to achieving that perfect rise an
 d flavor. We’ll dive into various techniques for shaping your loaves\, f
 rom classic rounds to unique designs.Learn how to customize your sourdough
  with unique ingredients\, adding a personal touch to your creations. You
 ’ll also explore different scoring methods to achieve beautiful patterns
  on your bread. Each participant will leave with a starter culture to kick
 start their sourdough journey\, their own ready-to-bake boule\, and the co
 nfidence to bake their own sourdough!
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/introduction-to-sourdough-b
 aking-august/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:No Cell Sundays: P-Butta
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260809T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260809T143000
UID:260728uhQzl2X0X0OuT81JvtCfHQ
DESCRIPTION:**Unplug and Groove: P-Butta Live at the Vineyard**\n\nJoin us
  for No Cell Sundays with P-Butta\, a local powerhouse trio that's been ma
 king Sonoma County move for decades.\n\nP-Butta is the instrumental side p
 roject of the musicians from Rising Tide\, the original Groundation band. 
 With Marcus Urani on keyboards\, Ryan Newman on bass\, and Paul Spina on d
 rums\, this three-piece brings together four decades of funk\, soul\, and 
 jazz mastery that satisfies any musical palate.\n\nExpect to hear groovy c
 overs from legendary artists like The Meters\, Booker T & the M.G.'s\, Her
 bie Hancock\, Donnie Hathaway\, Cannonball Adderley\, and even the Beastie
  Boys. Whether you're a jazz head or just love good vibes\, P-Butta delive
 rs the perfect soundtrack for a Sunday afternoon in wine country.\n\n**Wha
 t's No Cell Sundays?**\n\nIt's simple: disconnect from your devices\, reco
 nnect with great wine\, live music\, and the people around you. *Check yo
 ur phone with us at the door and receive a complimentary tasting.* Bring 
 a blanket\, grab a glass\, and spend your Sunday the way it was meant to b
 e spent.
LOCATION:Hook & Ladder Winery
URL:https://www.hookandladderwinery.com/event/no-cell-sundays-p-butta
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
