BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma Sundays on the Plaza - Tim Weed Trio & The Dorian Mode
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260809T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260809T170000
UID:260508o3Xit2TwK0GA7g7yu7M3uA
DESCRIPTION:This summer\, Music in Place and the City of Sonoma invite you
  to soak up the sunshine\, sip local wine\, and dance to live music at the
  Sonoma Plaza Grinstead Amphitheater during Sonoma Sundays On the Plaza\, 
 a free concert series running June 7 through October 4\, 2026.\n\nThis wee
 k's lineup features Time Weed and The Dorian Mode! Tim Weed is a lifelong\
 , Grammy-nominated concert musician\, composer\, producer\, recording engi
 neer\, and recording artist. Best known for his virtuosity on the 5-string
  banjo\, songwriting\, and soaring vocals. The doRiaN Mode explores the Gr
 eat American Songbook as it dishes up vintage jazz\, swinging R&B\, and so
 ulful ballads\, from the sassy sounds of 1920s speakeasies and 1930s big-b
 and swing to 1940s jump blues and the rollicking R&B of Ruth Brown. Vocali
 st and bassist Dorian Bartley leads this Petaluma-based acoustic quartet f
 eaturing Robby Elfman on piano/clarinet\, Peter Graves on sax\, and Tony B
 lake on drums. \n\nSonoma Sundays are free and open to all\, thanks to th
 e generous support of the Sonoma Community Center\, The Dawn Redwoods Trus
 t\, and the McNeely Family Foundation.\n\nPack your picnic\, bring your da
 ncing shoes\, and meet us on the Plaza!
