DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260811T200000
UID:260803qAW6kcmglUuyaFYV0MBPvQ
DESCRIPTION:✨ Join Us for the Next Young Petaluma Woman's Club Gathering
 ! ✨\n\nWe're excited to welcome Melissa Franks\, a 2024 Top 100 COO Awar
 d Winner and dynamic speaker\, for an evening of inspiration\, connection\
 , and practical leadership insights.\n\n🎤 Featured Presentation:\n\nThe
  Founder Bottleneck: Why Everything Runs Through You (and How to Fix It)\n
 \nWhether you're running a business\, leading a team\, balancing a busy ca
 reer\, or simply feeling like you're carrying too much\, Melissa will shar
 e actionable strategies to:\n\n✨ Create better systems\n\n✨ Build trus
 t and empower others\n\n✨ Focus on what matters most\n\nEnjoy a deliciou
 s catered dinner from Petaluma Market (vegan option available)\, wine\, an
 d meaningful networking with incredible women from our community.\n\n📅 
 Evening Schedule\n\n🕠 5:30 PM – Networking & Social Hour\n\n🕕 6:00
  PM – Dinner\n\n🕡 6:30 PM – Melissa Franks Presentation & Q&A\n\n
 🕢 7:30 PM – Wrap-Up\n\n💜 We'd love to see you there! If you've bee
 n thinking about joining us\, now's the perfect time. Feel free to invite 
 a friend—guests are always welcome!\n\n📩 Please RSVP by August 5 so w
 e can finalize our  dinner count.\n\ncourtney.kimble@n2co.com\n\nWe can't
  wait to connect\, learn\, and grow together. See you soon! 🌟\n\nwww.pe
 talumawomansclub.com\n\n#YoungPetalumaWomansClub #PetalumaWomansClub #Wome
 nSupportingWomen #Leadership #Networking #WomenInBusiness #Community #Peta
 luma #ProfessionalDevelopment #WomenLeaders
LOCATION:Petaluma Woman's Club
URL:http://www.petalumawomansclub.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Deep Dive into Soda Firing with Dan Clauson
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260811T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260811T130000
UID:260803ZbNdNJSRW0uaQjydnttkRQ
DESCRIPTION:Tuesdays\, August 11 – September 1\, 2026\n\n10:00 AM – 1:
 00 PM\n\nWeekend Long Firing Workshop\n\nSaturday\, September 12\, 2026 10
 :00 AM – 5:00 PM\n\nSunday\, September 13\, 2026 4:00 PM – 7:00 PM\n\n
 Location\n\nRoom 117\, Ceramics Studio\n\nCategory\n\nCeramics\, Extended 
 Classes\n\nExperience Level\n\nIntermediate\n\nAges\n\n17\\+\n\nRegistrati
 on Cost:\n\n$320\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\nIncluded\n\nTotal Registration Cost:
 \n\n$320\n\nIn this 4 session intensive\, students will create work for a 
 soda firing while learning the history and chemistry of atmospheric Soda. 
 Each session there will be demos and assignments that will lend to intenti
 onal and experimental decisions on the objects we make for the firing. We 
 will make tests in clay material\, slips\, glazes\, experiment in wadding\
 , and placements in the kiln. During class there will be lectures on the c
 hemistry of clay and of soda firing as well as its history\, application\,
  and experiments within the field. This class is about learning how to exp
 lore what soda can do.During the 4 weeks each student will create one cubi
 c foot of work to be bisqued and then fired in the soda kiln. The firing 
 will be two full days of activity\, with students applying the lessons lea
 rned in class to the wadding and loading of the kiln and lighting the kiln
 . Students will learn how to plan a gas kiln schedule\, use a kiln log\, a
 ssess a kilns needs\, and successfully fire off a kiln. Students will lear
 n how to spray soda and how to maintain the kiln and her accessories in or
 der to support Julia’s \\(our beloved soda kiln\\) longevity. This deep
  dive into soda will spark ideas and expand folx knowledge on kilns\, firi
 ng\, and making in clay.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/deep-dive-into-soda-firing-
 with-dan-clauson/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jewish Film Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260811T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260811T183000
UID:260802fIu2B4fdxECzN5d_26wWyA
DESCRIPTION:Don't miss one of the summers funniest movies! **The JCC’s J
 ewish Film Festival presents *The Floaters* on Tuesday August 11 at 1 an
 d 6:30 pm.** The Floaters is a warm-hearted R-rated Jewish summer camp com
 edy that’s winning over critics with its authentic cultural comedy and s
 trong ensemble cast. Reviewers are calling it entertaining\, funny and sur
 prisingly sincere. Seligfilmnews.com says that “this is a fun watch and 
 I was a little sad when it was over\,” And “I am sure there are bits I
  missed as a non-Jewish person\, but the film never made me feel like that
 . There is enough context given in areas that most people who were not rai
 sed in the faith or community can follow and do not feel like an outsider 
 looking in.” “The Floaters is charming\, funny\, sincere and unexpecte
 dly touching. The writing s excellent\, it’s a really enjoyable story wi
 th plenty of nostalgic touches.” …*Film Carnage*   In other words\, t
 his is a film for everyone. Get your tickets for this feel-good summer com
 edy at rialtocinemas.com.
LOCATION:Rialto Cinemas Sebastopol
URL:http://jccsoco.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
