BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Caesar - Shakespeare in the Park(ing Lot)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260814T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260814T211500
UID:2607035fKoVhsRDE2lUSDUXFChmQ
DESCRIPTION:Free Shakespeare in the Park\\(ing Lot\\). Elections\, ego\, f
 ear. Caesar climbs. The republic fractures.\n\nWe are excited to announce 
 ‘Shakespeare in the Park\\(ing Lot\\)’ 2026.\n\nFree Shakespeare.\n\nC
 aesar\n\nPresented by the Jacobethan Theatre Workshop.\n\nDoors open at 6
 .75pm\, performance at 7.30pm.\n\nOn Sundays\, doors open at 2.15pm with a
 s 3pm start.\n\nDirected by Lukas Raphael\n\nCaesar unfolds in 100 minute
 s of sharp\, modern storytelling. A political system strains under ambitio
 n\, loyalty fractures\, and public rhetoric turns volatile. With minimal s
 taging and contemporary dress\, the play lands uncomfortably close to the 
 present: a study of power\, perception\, and how quickly a republic can sh
 ift.\n\nNo intermission.\n\nA local selection of wine and beer can be purc
 hased in the theater.
LOCATION:Life On Art
URL:https://www.jacobethan.org/parking-lot
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
