SUMMARY:10 Things You Need to Know About Redwood Writers and Writing a Boo
 k
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T133000
UID:260803zxl8AAihSEuGrve7BTi6Dw
DESCRIPTION:Are you looking for a writing club of nice people willing to h
 elp you write your first \\(or next\\) book? Or are you new to Redwood Wri
 ters? We're Sonoma County's branch of the California Writers Club — and 
 as the largest writing club in California\, we support writers at any leve
 l. Our mission is writers helping writers\, and we'd love to meet you.\n\n
 This month's gathering will serve as an introduction to Redwood Writers\, 
 showcasing the many opportunities available within our branch and the grea
 ter California Writers Club. You'll get a preview of the exciting events a
 nd happenings planned for the year ahead — including our upcoming Sonoma
  County Writers Conference on October 17\, 2026 — along with ways you ca
 n get more involved.\n\nWe'll round out the meeting with a few writing exe
 rcises\, just to get the ink flowing.\n\nBest of all\, if you bring a frie
 nd\, both of you get in free!\n\nBetter yet\, bring a friend and a dish to
  share when we network during the break.\n\nWe hope you'll join us and dis
 cover how Redwood Writers can inspire\, connect\, and support you on your 
 writing journey.
LOCATION:Finley Center
URL:https://redwoodwriters.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mexican American Vintners Association's 14th Annual La Cosecha
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T210000
UID:260803d8lK_0_bSkqfYD4HSIEBdw
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Wine\, Culture & Community at the 14th Annual La Cos
 echa Grand Tasting\n\nJoin the Mexican American Vintners Association \\(MA
 VA\\) for an unforgettable summer evening celebrating the vibrant spirit\,
  rich heritage\, and exceptional craftsmanship of Mexican-American winemak
 ers at the 14th Annual La Cosecha Grand Tasting.\n\nSet against the beauti
 ful patio setting at Heirs of My Dream Winery in Sonoma\, this signature e
 vent brings together acclaimed MAVA member wineries\, culinary experiences
 \, live entertainment\, and community for an immersive wine country celebr
 ation unlike any other.\n\nSpend the afternoon tasting exceptional handcra
 fted wines from Mexican-American-owned wineries across California while en
 joying Latino-inspired cuisine\, live acoustic music\, and meaningful conn
 ections with the vintners\, growers\, and families behind the labels. As t
 he sun sets\, the evening transitions into an energetic after-party experi
 ence featuring live music\, dancing\, and continued celebration under the 
 Sonoma sky.\n\nWhat Awaits You:\n\n🍷 Unlimited tastings from premier Me
 xican-American-owned wineries\n\n🌮 Delicious Latino-inspired culinary o
 fferings and small bites\n\n🎶 Live acoustic music during the Grand Tast
 ing\n\n✨ Meet the vintners\, growers\, and families shaping California w
 ine country\n\n🎁 Silent auction supporting MAVA’s scholarship and edu
 cation programs\n\n💃 Live band and after-party celebration from 6:00 PM
  to 9:00 PM\n\nEvent Details\n\nSaturday\, August 15\, 2026 4:30 PM – 9:
 00 PM PDT\n\nHeirs of My Dream Winery 22985 Burndale Road\, Buildings A & 
 B Sonoma\, CA 95476\n\nAttire: Wine Country Chic\n\n21\\+ Only | Rain or S
 hine\n\nEvent Schedule\n\n4:30 PM – Grand Tasting Begins Enjoy unlimited
  tastings from Mexican-American-owned wineries\, culinary offerings\, live
  acoustic music\, and opportunities to meet the winemakers.\n\n6:00 PM –
  After-Party Doors Open Guests who have purchased the After-Party Add-On m
 ay enter beginning at 6:00 PM to enjoy live music\, dancing\, and an eveni
 ng celebration of wine\, culture\, and community.\n\n6:00 PM – 9:00 PM 
 – Live Music & After-Party\n\n7:00 PM – Grand Tasting Concludes\n\n9:0
 0 PM – Event Ends\n\nTicket Information\n\nGeneral Admission – Grand T
 asting: $150 Includes unlimited wine tastings during the Grand Tasting exp
 erience from 4:30 PM – 7:00 PM.\n\nAfter-Party Add-On: $50\n\nContinue t
 he celebration after the Grand Tasting with access to the After-Party begi
 nning at 6:00 PM. Admission includes two glasses of wine and live entertai
 nment.\n\nAdditional food and beverages will be available for purchase thr
 oughout the evening.\n\nDesignated Driver Ticket: $75\n\nWhether you’re 
 a devoted wine enthusiast\, an adventurous foodie\, or simply looking for 
 a memorable evening in Sonoma wine country\, La Cosecha offers a rare oppo
 rtunity to experience the passion\, culture\, and innovation driving one o
 f the wine industry’s most exciting communities.\n\nAbout MAVA\n\nThe Me
 xican American Vintners Association was founded to uplift\, support\, and 
 celebrate the contributions of Mexican-American vintners\, growers\, and i
 ndustry leaders. Proceeds from La Cosecha help fund scholarships\, educati
 onal initiatives\, and year-round programming supporting the next generati
 on of wine professionals.\n\nFollow Along\n\n@mava\\_wine | \\#LaCosecha20
 26 | nsmava.org\n\nSponsorship Inquiries: president@nvmava.org
LOCATION:Heirs of my Dream
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/1990529001828/preview/?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
