DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T210000
UID:260719B46pYVLym0K7hYGtNxjdiQ
DESCRIPTION:**On Saturday\, August 15 from 5–9 p.m.**\, **Little Saint**
 \, the 100% plant-based restaurant in Healdsburg\, and Michelin-recognized
  Italian restaurant\, **A16**\, are coming together for ***Tomato Sagra***
 : A one-night-only plant-based dinner celebrating Southern Italian traditi
 on and California's peak tomato season. \n\nTomato Sagra brings together 
 **Chef Deborah Mullin** of Little Saint and **Chef Valentin Atayde** of A1
 6 for a collaborative prix fixe dinner inspired by Southern Italy and Sono
 ma County's peak tomato season. Together\, the two culinary teams will sho
 wcase the season's juiciest\, sun-ripened tomatoes across a menu designed 
 to capture the magic of summer. Imagine dishes like cold-cured olive misti
  with pickled cherry tomatoes\, oven-dried cherry tomatoes on the vine\, A
 16's signature Naples-style pizza\, and more — all featuring ingredients
  sourced from Little Saint's eight-acre regenerative farm.
LOCATION:Little Saint
