BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:History Talks - Rails and Wheels
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T113000
UID:2605263hlAxx4r90ypFP7uKGxwLg
DESCRIPTION:Turn of the Century Transportation\n\nLearn about the Wild Wes
 t days of both rail and auto transportation in Healdsburg and Sonoma Count
 y in the late 19 th and early 20 th Century.\n\nMathew Lopez will tell tal
 es of the cut-throat race to establish the San Francisco & North Pacific R
 ailroad system in Sonoma County and its role in the formation of the much 
 larger Northwestern Pacific Railroad.\n\nDon Anderson will focus on transp
 ortation around town as it evolved from wagons\, livery stables and bicycl
 es to early automobiles\, commercial vehicles and buses. And how Healdsbur
 g became an automobile-centric destination with the opening of the Redwood
  Highway.
LOCATION:Healdsburg Plaza Gazebo
URL:https://www.healdsburgmuseum.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
