 n\nRoom 208\n\nCategory\n\nPrintmaking\n\nExperience Level\n\nBeginning\n\
 nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$300\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$
 50\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$350\n\nIn this special three-part works
 hop\, participants will be introduced to the art of Japanese woodblock pri
 nting called Ukiyo-E technique. Tomoko Murakami\, an acclaimed Bay Area\, 
 Japanese-born printmaking artist\, will demonstrate the traditional Mokuha
 nga carving and printing process. Tomoko will introduce the relationship b
 etween positive and negative space in relief printing techniques\, includi
 ng Kento registration. Participants will learn to carve their own woodbloc
 ks using Japanese carving tools to create small multi-color woodblocks and
  create prints with non-toxic water-based inks on Japanese paper. Students
  will be able to develop an appreciation of Japanese woodblock prints\, ma
 terials\, processes and innovations. Learn to carve your own woodblocks an
 d create a small edition of multicolor prints! This class is perfect for b
 eginners as well as continuing students. All levels are welcome!Please not
 e: This class requires hand dexterity to maneuver the carving tools. Parti
 cipants should feel comfortable standing and using wood carving tools with
  sharp blades and edges.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/mokuhanga-japanese-woodbloc
 k-printmaking/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:No Cell Sundays: Callie Watts & Kris Dilbeck
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260816T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260816T143000
UID:260728iyL1Kk9DSUq0N7CogXzf1g
DESCRIPTION:**Callie Watts: Where Classic Sounds Meet Modern Soul**\n\nJoi
 n us for No Cell Sundays with Callie Watts\, a Northern California pop sin
 ger-songwriter whose sound is steeped in the golden era of songwriting.\n\
 nRaised on classical music\, The Beatles\, and The Beach Boys\, Callie dis
 covered her calling through the great writers of the '60s and '70s—Joni 
 Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy Joel\, and Caro
 le King. These legendary artists shaped her melodic writing style and cont
 inue to influence every note she plays.\n\nA versatile musician\, Callie h
 as spent her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, arranger\, and
  lead/backing vocalist—performing solo and with local and Bay Area bands
  across multiple genres. Expect an afternoon of soulful melodies\, timeles
 s classics\, and songs that transport you back to when music was everythin
 g.\n\n**What's No Cell Sundays?**\n\nIt's simple: disconnect from your dev
 ices\, reconnect with great wine\, live music\, and the people around you.
  *Check your phone with us at the door and receive a complimentary tasting
 .* Bring a blanket\, grab a glass\, and spend your Sunday the way it was m
 eant to be spent.
LOCATION:Hook & Ladder Winery
URL:https://www.hookandladderwinery.com/event/no-cell-sundays-callie-watts
 -kris-dilbeck
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
