BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:4-Week Beginner Cumbia Series Program with Mireille - August
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260818T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260818T193000
UID:260720TUrD1VJIlUOjcigHHru2kw
DESCRIPTION:AUGUST 18 – SEPTEMBER 8\n\nFeel the Rhythm with Cumbia\n\nRe
 ady to master the “Step of the Soul”? Join us for a high-energy cumbia
  class where we dive into the heart of Latin America’s most infectious d
 ance. Whether you have two left feet or you’re a dance floor regular\, t
 his class will get you moving with confidence.\n\nMireille will guide you 
 through:\n\n4-Week Beginner Cumbia Series Program\n\nWeek 1 – Foundation
 s & Rhythm\n\n• Introduction to cumbia music and timing\n\n• Basic ste
 ps \\( tropical and sonidera basics \\)\n\n• Understanding the beat \\( 
 quick quick slow – quick quick slow \\)\n\n• Intro to partner connecti
 on \\(closed/open hold\\) ⸻\n\nWeek 2 – Footwork Development \\+ cumbi
 a Basic Turns\n\n• Review of basic step\n\n• Cumbia prep for turns\n\n
 • Traveling basics \\(moving around the floor\\)\n\n• Intro to basic c
 umbia turns .\n\n• Partner timing and frame basics\, partner work combin
 ation. ⸻\n\nWeek 3 – Styling & Partner Patterns\n\n• Review turns\n\
 n• Adding simple styling \\(arm movement\, body rhythm\\)\n\n• Cross-b
 ody lead variation \\(beginner-friendly\\)\n\n• Smooth transitions betwe
 en moves\n\n. Partner work combination. ⸻\n\nWeek 4 – Putting It All T
 ogether\n\n• Review all footwork and patterns\n\n• Combining moves int
 o a short sequence\n\n• Musicality: dancing with the music\n\n• Confid
 ence and flow on the dance floor\n\n• Social dancing practice \\+ mini r
 ecap\n\nImportant Details\n\nNo dance experience required: Whether you’v
 e never danced before or it’s been a while\, you’re welcome here!\n\nN
 o partner necessary: Come solo or bring a friend—either way\, you’ll h
 ave plenty of opportunities to dance.\n\nPlease wear non-marking shoe sole
 s: This helps us keep our dance floor in great condition.\n\nCome join us 
 and discover the joy of cumbia. We can’t wait to see you on the dance fl
 oor.\n\nDate & Time: Tuesdays \, 6:30 pm\n\n4-week course\, AUGUST 18 – 
 SEPTEMBER 8\n\nAugust 18th\, August 25th\, September 1st\, September 8th\n
 \nInstructor: Mireille Ruiz Born and raised in Mexico City\, she grew up d
 ancing and listening to Latin Music as part of her culture including Cumbi
 a\, Banda\, ranchera\, quebradita\, etc. she learned her first following T
 echniques\, dancing with her father in every family fiesta. she has a back
 ground in Mexican folklore\, Jazz\, tap dancing and gymnastics\, she also 
 is a percussionist\, drummer and Montessori Teacher.\n\nShe grew up perfor
 ming since she the age of 4. Bay Area bachata and cumbia dance instructor\
 , Mireille has been teaching dance\, performing\, leading dance teams\, ar
 ound USA events\, dance festivals\, congresses since 2008\n\nAddress: 4140
  Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafael\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. N
 o floor marking shoe soles allowed.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/cumbia/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gamble Estates Sauvignon Blanc Experience
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260818T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260818T140000
UID:260720IYHRKAfVikmQ28wu1T5HuA
DESCRIPTION:Seasonal Offering Through September 2026\n\nExplore a new dime
 nsion of Napa Valley Sauvignon Blanc through this seasonal tasting experie
 nce. Begin with a glass of the 2025 Yountville Sauvignon Blanc as you’re
  guided through the cellar\, exploring the cigar\, puncheon\, and barrique
  barrels used in our Reserve program.\n\nThen\, take a seat in our vineyar
 d‑facing salon for a guided exploration of the 2023\, 2024\, and 2025 Yo
 untville Sauvignon Blanc. Your tasting will conclude with our Reserve Sauv
 ignon Blanc\, offering a deeper look at the craft and progression behind t
 his signature wine.\n\n*Tasting fees are applied toward wine purchases.*
LOCATION:Gamble Estates 
URL:https://gambleestates.com/reservation/type/sauvignon-blanc-experience/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Intermediate Cumbia with Mireille
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260818T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260818T203000
UID:260718HTANCVHh80ym4_RJ50_Rtg
DESCRIPTION:4-Week Series | Tuesdays at 7:30 PM\n\nAUGUST 18 – SEPTEMBER
  8\n\nTake Your Cumbia to the Next Level Ready to level up your “Step of
  the Soul”? Join us for a high-energy\, Intermediate Cumbia series desig
 ned to take you beyond the basics and inject flavor\, intricate patterns\,
  and advanced musicality into your dance. If you are comfortable with the 
 basic rhythm and ready to challenge your footwork and partner work\, this 
 class is for you!\n\nPrerequisite: Completion of the Beginner Cumbia serie
 s \\(or equivalent foundational experience\\) is required.\n\n4-Week Inter
 mediate Cumbia Series Program Week 1 – Intermediate Foundations & Comple
 x Timing\n\nQuick review of basic steps \\(Tropical and Sonidera\\) and rh
 ythm check\n\nIntroduction to syncopated footwork and advanced timing shif
 ts\n\nEnhancing partner connection: tension\, compression\, and frame cont
 rol for faster transitions\n\nIntermediate partner work combination with d
 ynamic direction changes\n\nWeek 2 – Advanced Turns\, Traveling\, & Prec
 ision\n\nReview of Week 1 combination and footwork\n\nMultiple turns and a
 ccelerated turn preparations for both leaders and followers\n\nAdvanced tr
 aveling basics: mastering floor craft and moving effortlessly across the r
 oom\n\nComplex partner patterns incorporating intricate hand-drops and loo
 ps\n\nWeek 3 – Styling\, Body Isolation\, & Intricate Patterns\n\nReview
  of advanced turns and loops\n\nAdding intermediate styling: body isolatio
 ns\, hip action\, and expressive arm styling\n\nAdvanced cross-body lead v
 ariations and continuous turn combinations\n\nDeveloping smooth\, seamless
  transitions between complex moves\n\nWeek 4 – Musicality\, Flow\, & Soc
 ial Mastery\n\nReview of all intermediate footwork\, styling\, and pattern
 s\n\nCombining the 4-week material into an advanced choreography sequence\
 n\nDeep dive into musicality: hitting the breaks\, accents\, and interpret
 ing different Cumbia sub-genres\n\nBuilding confidence\, flow\, and expres
 sion for the social dance floor\n\nSocial dancing practice \\+ comprehensi
 ve mini recap\n\nImportant Details\n\nExperience Level: Intermediate. Begi
 nner class/foundational experience is required.\n\nNo partner necessary: C
 ome solo or bring a friend—we will rotate throughout the class so everyo
 ne gets plenty of time to dance.\n\nFootwear: Please wear non-marking shoe
  soles to help us keep our dance floor in great condition.\n\nArrival: Ple
 ase arrive 10 minutes before class starts.\n\nDate & Time: Tuesdays\, 7:30
  PM \\(4-week course\, AUGUST 18 – SEPTEMBER 8\\)\n\nAugust 18th\, Augus
 t 25th\, September 1st\, September 8th\n\nAbout the Instructor: Mireille R
 uiz\n\nBorn and raised in Mexico City\, Mireille grew up immersed in the m
 usic and dance of her culture\, including Cumbia\, Banda\, Ranchera\, and 
 Quebradita. She learned her first following techniques dancing with her fa
 ther at family fiestas.\n\nWith a rich background in Mexican folklore\, Ja
 zz\, tap dancing\, and gymnastics\, Mireille is also a percussionist\, dru
 mmer\, and Montessori Teacher. She has been performing since the age of 4.
  As a premier Bay Area Bachata and Cumbia instructor\, Mireille has been t
 eaching dance\, performing\, and leading dance teams at major USA events\,
  festivals\, and congresses since 2008.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/intermediate-cumbia/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Painting in Fauve
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260818T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260818T180000
UID:260715hAimeySJ_kSycKy2BpNzyw
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  7/15/26\n\n**AUGUST EXHIBIT: PAI
 NTING IN FAUVE**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  **July 27 – August 30\, 2026**\n\n*
 *RECEPTION: SATURDAY\, August 1\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Willow La
 Land and Gen Zorich\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show.  Be
  sure to take part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beautif
 ul work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSonoma wi
 ne country artist\, **Willow LaLand** presents **Painting in Fauve\,** a c
 ollection of oil and acrylic paintings focusing on our region’s vibrant 
 beauty through the artist’s Fauvist lens.  Known for her hyper-realisti
 c landscapes\, these works take an imaginative turn to the fantastical\, t
 apping into the wild Fauve vivid color palette.   Highlighting the show\
 , “Mt. Tamalpais” comes alive\, swathed in rich colors cascading over 
 its undulating slopes\, while rich foreground purple/blues heighten the mo
 untain’s grandeur.  “Fitch Mountain” similarly seems to sing with c
 olor as it overlooks a lush vineyard.  LaLand’s color lens takes us fro
 m palette to palate as she captures the luxuriant purple/reds of a fine re
 d wine in “Sommelier’s Dream.”  Reflecting on her creative process\
 , LaLand notes “I love the artistic freedom to play\, create depth in co
 lor\, and give a tangible realistic impression within a completely fantast
 ical expression.”\n\nA third-generation artist\, LaLand started her stud
 ies as a young girl and had a studio space at 10 years old.  She is inspi
 red by early American realists and uses traditional techniques to achieve 
 dramatic realism.  LaLand finds the Fauve color palette elicits a joyful 
 response to her themes of nature and wine.  Many of her collectors love b
 oth her styles and have a hard time\, though they vastly differ\, choosing
  between the two.  LaLand exhibits widely\, including internationally\, a
 nd participated in the Art Trails Program.  She was featured in American 
 Art Collector magazine in 2013 and on KRCB in 2015.\n\nMeet the artist: La
 Land will host the Gallery on August 2\, 2:30 – 6pm and August 16 & 29\,
  11am to 6 pm.\n\nThe Stairway Smallworks Showcase features **Gen Zorich
 ’s Summertime\,** highlighting the beauty of wine country and the warmth
  of long\, lazy summer days.  From Zorich’s background as a geologist a
 nd environmental scientist\, she imbues her paintings with a deep understa
 nding of the natural world. Focusing on flora\, pink waterlilies floating 
 on pastel pads in “Summer Color” engender a sense of sun-filled easy d
 ays.  These works would bring a feeling of summer contentment any time of
  year.  An award-winning artist\, Zorich has exhibited widely and has bee
 n a longtime participant in the Sonoma County Art Trails Program.\n\nMeet 
 the artist: Zorich will host the Gallery on August 2\, 11am – 2:30pm\, A
 ugust 4\, 11am to 6 pm and August 21 & 23\, 2:30 – 6pm.\n\nAlso join us 
 for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\, August 6\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE
  Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community event 
 celebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participating. This 
 month’s special theme: Music and Mocktails.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\n
 Upstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 43
 1-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **www.upstairsart gallery.net** 
 \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bv
 drio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Galler
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
