 ptember 23\, 2026\n\n6:00 PM – 9:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 117\, Ceramic
 s Studio\n\nCategory\n\nCeramics\, Extended Classes\n\nExperience Level\n\
 nAdvanced\n\nAges\n\n17+\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$265\n\nMaterials Fee:\n
 \n$30\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$295\n\nThis session is designed for 
 people who have already taken multiple wheel throwing courses. A continuat
 ion of our intermediate course\, this upper level / advanced course will h
 elp you hone your throwing skills through more complex demos\, and nuanced
  approaches to technical throwing. In this 8 week course\, students will d
 ive deep into developing their own unique voice as they build a technical 
 toolset for the independent maker. In addition to throwing\, surface decor
 ation techniques will be explored as well as the opportunity to experiment
  with different clay bodies.With your 8 week class registration\, students
  receive the opportunity to purchase a studio pass for ½ off during the d
 uration of their class. Sign ups for membership will be included.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/pottery-on-the-wheel-advanc
 ed-august/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
