BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beneath the Trees: A Day of Creative Wellness With Ali McKleroy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260820T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260820T163000
UID:2607274n3AkKX4A0qjbHZWVXS1-g
DESCRIPTION:Beneath the Trees: A Day of Creative Wellness is a workshop fo
 r those who spend their days holding space for others and are ready to be 
 held themselves\, by community\, by creativity\, and by nature. Gathered o
 utdoors beneath a canopy of trees\, near a stream\, you’ll use creativit
 y as a portal to insight\, energy\, and renewal. Through expressive arts\,
  creative mindfulness\, and intuitive art-making woven into the natural wo
 rld around you\, you’ll release what’s been weighing you down\, reigni
 te your spark\, and return to a lightness of being. For healers\, helpers\
 , seekers\, and anyone running on empty. You’ll leave feeling grounded\,
  creatively alive\, and quietly restored by the woods.  \n\nYour morning 
 begins with a creative workshop held outdoors beneath the trees\, explorin
 g arts-based and nature-based practices\, creative mindfulness\, and art-m
 aking that open a pathway to intuitive wisdom\, emotional release\, and a 
 renewed sense of aliveness.  \n\nIn the afternoon\, you’ll sink into de
 ep renewal: \n\nCedar enzyme footbath\n\n70-minute massage or 65-minute fa
 cial\n\nWalking meditation through a bamboo forest\n\nGuided meditation in
  a Japanese garden\n\nA nourishing lunch by a local chef\, served creeksid
 e beneath ancient oaks\n\nAbout Ali \n\nAli McKleroy\, M.A.\, LMFT\, is a 
 licensed art therapist\, author\, and mindfulness teacher with over 20 yea
 rs of experience helping people shed what dims them and reconnect with the
 ir creative vitality. Her work weaves together expressive arts\, creative 
 mindfulness\, and deep listening to unlock the wisdom and energy already w
 ithin you. Alison is the author of The Self-Compassion Journal and Essenti
 al Strategies for Social Anxiety\, and has been featured in TIME\, The Gua
 rdian\, Forbes\, Well\\+Good\, Verywell Mind\, DailyOM\, HuffPost\, and mo
 re. She brings warmth\, humor\, and a grounded presence to her workshops. 
 \n\nJoin Us!
URL:https://osmosis.com/event/beneath-the-trees-a-day-of-creative-wellness
 /
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
