BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Josh Flores: Big Feels - Featured August Artist in the Living Room
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260821T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260821T170000
UID:260804wenNs-zgFESMtVeM-O-Gqw
DESCRIPTION:The San Geronimo Valley Community Center proudly presents the 
 artwork of **Josh Flores** in the Living Room of the Maurice Del Mue Gal
 leries. There will be a reception for the artist on **August 9 from 2 - 4
  pm**. \n\nJosh has previously exhibited work in the San Rafael Youth In 
 Arts Program  “What About Age?” exhibit at the Marin Civic Center and
  the “One If By Land\, Two if By Sea” show at the Bolinas Art Museum.
  This is Josh’s first solo exhibition at the Community Center.\n\n**Art
 ist bio:** Josh Flores was born in Lima\, Peru and raised in Marin. He ap
 preciates the experience of taking a blank piece of paper and going throug
 h the process of making something as a reminder to himself that he is capa
 ble of anything. His earliest influence to make art came from watching ama
 teur anime\, reading manga and his first art teacher Mr. Powell.\n\n**Arti
 st statement:** Titled “BIG Feels” the inspiration for his first solo
  show came from his recent birthday\, when he experienced emotional sadnes
 s related to fear of abandonment. He created the first piece titled “Sad
  Boi Birthday” to illustrate the depth of the emotion he was feeling. Ea
 ch piece is created with a graphite sketch followed by ink and alcohol mar
 ker.
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sangeronimovalleycommunitycenter.eventcalendarapp.com/josh-flo
 res-big-feels-featured-august-artist-in-the-living-room
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
