BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nature Linocut
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260826T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260826T200000
UID:260728jhVuFSV-kUGyxbxoj10wbQ
DESCRIPTION:Every Wednesday · 3 Weeks\n\nDate & Time\n\nAugust 12 – 26\
 , 2026\n\n5:30 PM – 8:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nFirst session at Sonoma Garde
 n Park Following sessions in Room 208\n\nCategory\n\nPrintmaking\n\nExperi
 ence Level\n\nBeginning\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$
 140\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$25\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$165\n\nIn thi
 s fun\, introductory series\, journey into the world of linocut printmakin
 g by exploring nature and the foundational principles and techniques used 
 in block printing.In this class\, participants will begin with a short nat
 ure photo walk at the Sonoma Garden Park for field inspiration. Students w
 ill then head into the printmaking studio where they will have the opportu
 nity to explore block printing through a series of exercises geared toward
 s converting a photograph or a pencil sketch into a contemporary linoleum 
 print. Guests will learn to carve and print a 4 x 6 inch rubber block usin
 g a carving tool\, and non-toxic water-soluble inks to create a small seri
 es of creative block prints and hand-printed cards with a variety of paper
  choices. No experience is required. This is a guided and paced process w
 ith three consecutive class meetings. This workshop is great for anyone ne
 w to relief block carving\, and for those who may already have some beginn
 ing experience in printmaking they want to expand on. Whether you’re new
  to print\, or looking to brush up your skills\, this hands-on workshop of
 fers a supportive space to create some truly beautiful nature prints!Pleas
 e note: This class requires some walking\, and hand dexterity to maneuver 
 the carving tools. Participants should feel comfortable meeting onsite at 
 the Garden Park for the initial first class meeting. Students should also 
 feel comfortable using tools with sharp blades and edges.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/nature-linocut/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Creative Seasonal Cooking with Erin Shallat
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260826T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260826T113000
UID:260728iCmtKrvijUmUeva8XZ1sEA
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nMonday & Wednesday · Weekly\n\nDate & Time\n\nAug
 ust 3 – 26\, 2026\n\n10:00 AM – 11:30 AM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 109\, Rot
 ary Kitchen\n\nCategory\n\nCulinary Arts\, Wellness\n\nExperience Level\n\
 nBeginning\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration Cost Per Class:\n\n$10\
 n\nMaterials Fee:\n\nIncluded\n\nTotal Registration Cost Per Class:\n\n$10
 \n\nDiscover the joy of cooking with beautiful\, locally grown produce in 
 a relaxed\, inspiring kitchen environment. These intimate classes are desi
 gned to spark creativity\, build confidence\, and make everyday meal prep 
 feel simple\, sustainable\, and deeply satisfying. Classes are offered two
  times per week on Monday and Wednesdays from 10:00–11:30 AM throughout 
 August\, followed by a casual lunch and Q&A where guests can connect\, ask
  questions\, and continue the conversation around food\, wellness\, and se
 asonal living. Rather than a formal step-by-step cooking course\, each ses
 sion is primarily demonstration-based with occasional hands-on participati
 on. Every class highlights a seasonal fruit or vegetable and explores seve
 ral delicious ways to prepare and enjoy it using fresh\, vibrant ingredien
 ts. The first class focuses on creating a well-equipped kitchen for effort
 less meal prep\, including:\n\nSmart pantry\, refrigerator\, and freezer s
 tocking\n\nEssential cooking tools and equipment\n\nOrganizing for ease an
 d efficiency\n\nSetting up a kitchen that supports healthy\, creative cook
 ing\n\nWith produce harvested from Erin’s own gardens\, participants wil
 l experience an abundance of fresh seasonal ingredients while learning app
 roachable techniques and flavorful recipes that can easily be recreated at
  home. Classes are  welcoming\, personal experience with plenty of opport
 unity for questions\, conversation\, and inspiration. Simple. Fresh. Creat
 ive. Nourishing cooking without the fuss.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/creative-seasonal-cooking-w
 ith-erin-shallat/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
