BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Equivocation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T193000
UID:260803NKh1OnLWfEyo7dBVRBZYVg
DESCRIPTION:England\, 1605: A terrorist plot is brewing to assassinate Kin
 g James 1 and blow Parliament to kingdom come! Or so the King claims. To s
 pread his propaganda\, King James 1 hires the world’s most famous playwr
 ight\, William Shagspeare \\(after a contemporary spelling of the Bard’s
  name\\). As Shag investigates the King’s bizarre tale\, he begins to qu
 estion it\, leading him and his actors to a dilemma: lie and pocket the ca
 sh\, tell the truth and literally risk their necks\, or perhaps equivocate
 –lie and tell the truth at the same time. This high-stakes thriller drop
 s into many of the Bard’s most famous works in an alternate history that
  resonates today. This is a witty and poignant ensemble piece in which six
  actors play well over a dozen roles\, some of which include snippets of S
 hakespeare's other plays-in-progress \\(one of which becomes the famous Ma
 cbeth.\\)
LOCATION:Spreckels Center for the Performing Arts
URL:https://spreckelsonline.com/show/2026-27-season/equivocation/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Michael Leonardi Foundation Music + Awareness Concert
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T190000
UID:260803NEvksDFcLUKE4WZKCEH8oQ
DESCRIPTION:Join us Saturday\, August 29\, 2026 for our next Michael Leona
 rdi Foundation Music \\+ Awareness Concert hosted at The Barn Napa Valley/
 Car Club in downtown Napa from 4-7 pm\, featuring Dirty Cello\, 945 The Ba
 nd and Cherry Blonde! This event features and supports talented musicians 
 while raising awareness about staying safe from illicit fentanyl. In addit
 ion to music\, the afternoon will also feature guest speakers and resource
 s\, a silent auction\, and food and beverages for purchase.\n\nReserve you
 r spot with at $30 donation through Eventbrite or at the door: https://MLF
 MusicAwareness2026.eventbrite.com\n\nA special thank you to our event spon
 sors Tugboat\, Cana Ranch and to our community supporters Napa County\, Na
 pa Health and Human Services Agency\, and the Matthew Perry Foundation.\n\
 nWe're thankful to The Barn Napa Valley / Car Club for partnering with us 
 to bring our community together for an evening of music and awareness.\n\n
 To learn more about our organization\, visit michaelleonardifoundation.org
 .\n\nThe Michael Leonardi Foundation is funded in part by Napa County Heal
 th and Human Services Agency \\(HHSA\\) through Opioid Settlement Funds \\
 (OSF\\) to support prevention\, intervention\, treatment\, recovery\, and 
 other life-saving programs and services for individuals and families throu
 ghout the community.
LOCATION:Napa Valley Car Club
URL:https://MLFMusicAwareness2026.eventbrite.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The TNG Reset - Why You Hurt Where You Do
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T111500
UID:260803GUB9GgODTUeYl1BU9tOffg
DESCRIPTION:If stretching provides only temporary relief—or sometimes ma
 kes you feel worse—the source of your discomfort may not be where you fe
 el the pain.\n\n**The TNG Reset** is an interactive\, small-group workshop
  designed to help you better understand your body’s compensation pattern
 s and recurring areas of tension.\n\nDuring the workshop\, you’ll explor
 e:\n\nWhy stretching doesn’t always work\n\nThe difference between a sho
 rtened muscle and one that is overstretched and exhausted\n\nHow posture\,
  movement habits\, the glutes\, and the psoas can contribute to recurring 
 tension\n\nTargeted ball-rolling and self-release techniques\n\nA realisti
 c five-minute reset routine you can use at home\n\nCome curious and wear c
 omfortable clothing. You’ll leave with practical tools and a clearer und
 erstanding of what may be contributing to your personal pain patterns.\n\n
 **Date:** Saturday\, August 29\, 2026 **Time:** 10:00–11:30 AM **Locatio
 n:** Shimmery Alchemy Studio **Address:** 406 E Street\, Santa Rosa **Pric
 e:** $60 per person **Led by:** Tiffany Gann of The Natural Gift Wellness 
 **Registration:** Advance registration required\; limited to 10 participan
 ts.
LOCATION:Shimmery Alchemy
URL:http://www.tngmassage.com/events
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:H&L Live: Frank and the Bone Machine
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T153000
UID:260728rRAGH_Cg1kKPHn47vhgnAg
DESCRIPTION:**H&L Live: Frank and the Bone Machine**\n\nFrank and the Bone
  Machine — a powerhouse North Bay ensemble celebrating the music of Tom 
 Waits.\n\nLed by musical director Paul Spina (drums)\, the group features 
 some of the region's most distinguished musicians: Jason Thwaits (guitar)\
 , Robby Elfman (sax\, clarinet\, keys\, and percussion)\, Ian Scherer (gui
 tar)\, Ben Dubin (bass and harmonica)\, and Devin Ruddick (vocals).\n\nTog
 ether they'll perform a hand-picked selection of their favorite cuts from 
 across the Tom Waits catalog — a rare evening of singular music set agai
 nst the backdrop of Sonoma County wine country.\n\n‍**What to Know:**\n\
 n**Admission is free** - just show up and enjoy\n\n**Outdoor seating** -
  lawn and picnic area available (bring blankets encouraged)\n\n**All ages 
 welcome** - family-friendly event\n\n**Wine available** for purchase by 
 the glass or bottle\n\nThis is H&L Live at its best: world-class musicians
 \, golden hour timing\, and the Russian River Valley as your backdrop. Com
 e early\, stay late\, and experience why the North Bay music scene is lege
 ndary.\n\n‍\n\n‍
LOCATION:Hook & Ladder Winery
URL:https://www.hookandladderwinery.com/event/hl-live-frank-and-the-bone-m
 achine
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
