BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Equivocation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260830T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260830T140000
UID:2608034ZVIhdxgEEqmPGkGstDkEQ
DESCRIPTION:England\, 1605: A terrorist plot is brewing to assassinate Kin
 g James 1 and blow Parliament to kingdom come! Or so the King claims. To s
 pread his propaganda\, King James 1 hires the world’s most famous playwr
 ight\, William Shagspeare \\(after a contemporary spelling of the Bard’s
  name\\). As Shag investigates the King’s bizarre tale\, he begins to qu
 estion it\, leading him and his actors to a dilemma: lie and pocket the ca
 sh\, tell the truth and literally risk their necks\, or perhaps equivocate
 –lie and tell the truth at the same time. This high-stakes thriller drop
 s into many of the Bard’s most famous works in an alternate history that
  resonates today. This is a witty and poignant ensemble piece in which six
  actors play well over a dozen roles\, some of which include snippets of S
 hakespeare's other plays-in-progress \\(one of which becomes the famous Ma
 cbeth.\\)
LOCATION:Spreckels Center for the Performing Arts
URL:https://spreckelsonline.com/show/2026-27-season/equivocation/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
