BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma Sundays on the Plaza - Marcos Silva
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260830T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260830T170000
UID:260529xYulV429zE-ybYAGes4aNA
DESCRIPTION:This summer\, Music in Place and the City of Sonoma invite you
  to soak up the sunshine\, sip local wine\, and dance to live music at the
  Sonoma Plaza Grinstead Amphitheater during Sonoma Sundays On the Plaza\, 
 a free concert series running June 7 through October 4\, 2026.\n\nThis wee
 k's lineup features Marcos Silva! Marcos Silva performs worldwide. He has 
 toured with many artists\, including Paquito D’Rivera\, Bud Shank\, Clau
 dio Roditi\, Raul de Souza\, Toninho Horta\, Leny Andrade\, Edu Lobo\, Emi
 lio Santiago\, and Dori Caymmi\, and he was the musical director for Flora
  Purim and Airto Moreira for 24 years. Silva has written arrangements for 
 Dizzy Gillespie’s band\, and he replaced Gil Evans as composer-arranger 
 of Airto’s Spiritual Mass with a 63-piece orchestra in Germany. He is al
 so sought after as a producer of albums\, including three of his own. Silv
 a’s composing was highlighted by the two albums he recorded with his sex
 tet Intersection for the Concord Records imprint Crossover. The first\, 19
 87’s Here We Go\, inspired Gil Evans to describe him as “a great compo
 ser and pianist.” Silva followed up with 1989’s Black & White\, anothe
 r session featuring all original compositions and arrangements. His alluri
 ng compositions have also been recorded by jazz giants such as Herbie Mann
 \, Toninho Horta\, Romero Lubambo\, Airto Moreira and Flora Purim.\n\nSono
 ma Sundays are free and open to all\, thanks to the generous support of th
 e Sonoma Community Center\, The Dawn Redwoods Trust\, and the McNeely Fami
 ly Foundation.\n\nPack your picnic\, bring your dancing shoes\, and meet u
 s on the Plaza!
LOCATION:Grinstead Amphitheater
URL:https://musicinplace.org/event/sonoma-sundays-on-the-plaza-8-30/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lynn Crossett
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260830T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260830T000000
UID:260327A5hVCm1zs0qRUyld5DHh3Q
DESCRIPTION:Lynn Crossett travels between Central Texas and Southern Calif
 ornia performing songwriting-focused Indie Americana music. In a follow-up
  to his 2022 album\, In the Company of a Song\, which debuted at No. 6 on 
 the Roots Music Report Top 50 Americana Country Album Chart and stayed in 
 the top 10 for eight weeks\, he is back working with Grammy Award-winning 
 producer Lloyd Maines on his latest release\, Autumn to August. Released o
 n June 20\, 2025\, the album debuted at No. 4 on the same chart and reache
 d No. 1 the following week.\n\n“Lynn Crossett pens songs about longtime 
 friendships\, realizations that come on over time\, and that nagging sensa
 tion that finding yourself isn’t about where you reside\, or where you r
 oam. They’re all brewed in a Texas style Americana.” \\(Elise Cady\, A
 mericana Highways\\)\n\nWith the release of Autumn to August\, Lynn is emb
 arking on a full-time music career and a more ambitious national and inter
 national touring schedule following his latest album release in June 2025.
LOCATION:Napa River Inn
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108050025?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
