UID:260713db9LO02UqUesD6G6X0gSHA
DESCRIPTION:Directions: Meet at the gate on San Andreas Dr in Novato. From
  Hwy 101 in Novato\, take the exit for San Marin Dr west 2.3 miles. Turn r
 ight onto San Andreas Dr and follow approximately 0.5 miles. The gate is o
 n the right \\(before dead end\\).\n\nSponsor: Parks\n\nAccommodation Info
 rmation: If you are a person with a disability and require an accommodatio
 n to participate in a County program\, service\, or activity\, req uests m
 ay be made by calling 415-473-4381 \\(Voice\\)\, Dial&nbs p\;711 for CA Re
 lay\, or by submitting a\n\nDisability Accommodation Request\n\nat least f
 ive business days in advance of the event. We will do our best to fulfill 
 requests received with less than five business days' notice. Copies of doc
 uments are available in alternative formats upon request.\n\nThere are man
 y ingenious creatures that have devised ways to trick plants into growing 
 structures\, called galls\, which shelter and feed them. We'll exa mine an
  amazing array of bizarre and beautiful galls as we learn the incredible l
 ife cycles of the gall makers. Total miles: 2. Elevation change: 275'. We'
 ll be off trail\, walking in tall grass part of the time\; pants and close
 d shoes recommended. Remember to bring lunch\, an d binoculars if you have
  them. No pets are allowed\, except for service/companion animals. Adverse
  weather or poor air quality may cancel . Registration is required.\n\nQue
 stions: Contact\n\nShannon Burke .
LOCATION:Mount
URL:https://www.marincounty.gov/county-marin-calendar
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
