BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Overeaters Anonymous (OA) Meeting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260830T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260830T103000
UID:260728nwtcMfcwfUuZ7eyb2J5e4w
DESCRIPTION:Is Food a Problem for You? You Are Not Alone.\n\nIn OA\, membe
 rs experience spiritual\, emotional\, and physical recovery by practicing 
 the Twelve Steps and living by their spiritual principles—one day at a t
 ime.\n\nOvereaters Anonymous \\(OA\\) is a fellowship of people who suppor
 t each other in recovering from compulsive eating and food behaviors. If y
 ou feel you have a problem with food\, OA welcomes you—no matter what yo
 ur background\, beliefs\, or eating habits. \n\nWe hold an in-person meet
 ings at 9:30 on Sunday mornings at Church of the Nazarene\, 18980 Arnold D
 rive\, Sonoma\, CA \\(a small room directly off of parking lot\; look for 
 the sign posted\\) and newcomers are always welcome.\n\nYou may view all N
 orth Bay OA in-person and online meetings at https://www.northbayoa.org/me
 etings.html\n\nOA is not a diet club or calorie-counting program.\n\nMembe
 rs have different plans of eating.\n\nOA does not endorse any specific foo
 d plan. \n\nVisit: https://www.northbayoa.org/\n\nFind a meeting: https:/
 /www.northbayoa.org/meetings.html
URL:https://www.northbayoa.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rare Tomato Tasting & Watercolor Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260830T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260830T170000
UID:260728n1ZWNKsbk0aBJEBkawSmAA
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a unique experience at Hope Acre farm\, offered on
 ce a month during the harvest season. Taste a selection of heirloom tomato
 es before learning to watercolor your favorites with local artist and wate
 rcolor teacher\, Hannah Day.\n\nHope Acre grows over 140 varieties of rare
  tomatoes\; with rare titles like “Indigo Blueberry” and “Rebel Star
  Fighter”\, your tasting will include a wide range of flavor profiles. Y
 ou will dine on tomatoes that look identical but taste opposite\, tomatoes
  named after beloved drag queens\, tomatoes smaller than marbles\, and oth
 ers larger than a softball. Your tomatoes will be served sun warm\, straig
 ht from the vine\, with local bread and cheese\, and presented with passio
 nate musing by farmer Jai\, whose knowledge is expansive and excitement is
  infectious.\n\nAfter your tasting\, you’ll spend time looking even clos
 er at your favorite selections of the farm’s yield. Seated in the farm
 ’s lush outdoor space\, instructor Hannah Day will walk you step by step
  through rendering your subjects with close observation\, foundational dra
 wing skills\, and a unique approach to watercolor technique. With a mix of
  demonstration and individual instruction\, artists of all experience leve
 ls can walk away with a meaningful creative experience.\n\nBYO wine or bev
 erage of choice ~ vegan cheese will be served along with dairy selections 
 ~ Please contact with other dietary concerns
LOCATION:Hope Acre Farm
URL:https://www.hannahdrawstrees.com/paint-and-taste-tomatoes
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
